  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#39704\", \"PowerToys#41229\"], \"answer\": \"This looks like a known limitation. PowerToys#39704 reports the same scenario: PowerToys runs as admin with the low-level keyboard hook on, an elevated app is focused, and the CmdPal shortcut doesn't work. The report there is that CmdPal doesn't respect its run_elevated preference. In PowerToys#41229 a maintainer said that anything running elevated (or Task Manager) ignores low-level keyboard hook hotkeys. With Win+S, that is why the default Windows Search opens instead. The tickets don't describe a fix. First check that 'Use low-level keyboard hook' is actually still enabled, since the person in #41229 had it toggled off by accident. If it is on, the Win+S shortcut will work when a non-elevated window is focused. It will not work over elevated windows until the issue is fixed. Please add your version (0.100.2) and your bug report to PowerToys#39704.\"}",
